@vsm 1.2.1
@status ratified
// s5-policy/vsl-language/standardization.vsm — tooling part of §19.
// Source: vsl_language §19 (vsl_standardization/spec.vsm). Item of the
// reference set. status_enum stays in boot/vsl_language_primer.vsm — NOT here.

standardization("VSL-LANG-STANDARDIZATION") {

  standardization: "
    single_source: task() block status: field is AUTHORITATIVE; session()
      blocks reference IDs (evidence, commits) but not only record of closure —
      reconcile writes closure back into task block.
    grammar: ONE task() form forward: task(\"ID\", priority=P, agent=[..],
      status=<enum>) = { ... }; legacy single-line read by validator, left in place
    validator (tasks_validate.py): flags (i) task missing/non-enum status
      (ii) DRIFT — done/resolved in session() but task() block not status=done
      (iii) duplicate IDs conflicting status. exit non-zero on any (ii)
    reconcile (tasks_reconcile.py --write): write session-block closure back
      into task block (status=done + closed_by: ref). 0 drift after.
    session_end_hook: tasks_validate.py in session-end checklist — session
      not ready to close if drift (mechanical, not vigilance)
    memory_index: MEMORY.md DERIVED from memory/*.md frontmatter (files =
      single source; index generated, not hand-edited). generator gen_index.py.
    v2 (only if v1 proves value): HANDOFF conformance + S3* timer.",
}
⟦ /standardization ⟧